- [ ] **[human-only]** Probe: Read pnpm-workspace.yaml and package.json for overrides and audit settings. Write: none. <!-- reconcile-id: template-put-pnpm-overrides-auditconfig-allow-076 --> Put pnpm `overrides` / `auditConfig` / `allowBuilds` in
      `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, **not** the `package.json` `pnpm` field — pnpm 10+
      ignores that field. Approve blocked build scripts (e.g. vite's `esbuild`,
      and `workerd` if deploying to Cloudflare Workers — else `wrangler deploy`
      fails `ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS`) via `allowBuilds` (pnpm 11+; the shipped
      `pnpm-workspace.yaml` uses it) or `pnpm approve-builds`. The `overrides`
      security-floor block is template-owned and arrives via `copier update`;
      add repository-local floors below its end marker, inside `overrides`,
      scoped to the line they floor (`pkg@<major>` bounded below the next major,
      or `pkg@0.<minor>` bounded below the next minor for 0.x, quoted for a
      scoped package: `'@scope/pkg@7': '>=7.0.1 <8'`). Every template floor
      follows this shape; the block never crosses a major. Write local floors
      with `task security:audit:fix` (the daily `security-audit-fix.yml` opens
      them as one rolling PR), never raw `pnpm audit --fix`: its selectors are
      unbounded across majors and it forces a major when the patch only exists
      there. Keep the file in the template's two-space indentation with both
      floor markers indented inside `overrides`; the task refuses a write that
      would reformat the block. For 0.x, selectors cover only the fixture
      graph's tested minors and bounds stop below the next minor of the moved
      version. A 0.x minor is moved only where upstream published no in-minor
      patch and the entry says so; the fixture toolchain builds with the moved
      versions. Other 0.x minor edges are left for consumer audit and a local
      floor after validation. When a later template version floors a release
      line you floored locally, delete your local entry. After a template update
      changes the block, run `pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile` and commit
      `pnpm-lock.yaml` — pnpm records the `overrides` in the lockfile, so a
      frozen install (for example, the CI setup action, `scripts/setup-remote.sh`,
      `task worktree:new`, or any shell with `CI` set) fails with
      `ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH` until the lockfile matches the block.
      Harmon Init's CI audits only its Astro fixture against the shipped block,
      not this app's graph: an advisory that exists only in the
      TanStack/Convex graph surfaces in this repository's own `pnpm audit`,
      so floor it locally with `task security:audit:fix` and report it
      upstream; an advisory on a release line the block already floors
      (its `pkg@<major>` or `pkg@0.<minor>` key) is refused there, so raise
      that one upstream instead.
